{"id":"18ad6e37d70b294d","group":"58","path":"58/batch09/58-df-product-measure.md","title":"Product Measure","display":"df-product-measure — Product Measure","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-product-measure","aliases":["58-df-product-measure","Product Measure"],"display":"df-product-measure — Product Measure","depends_on":["[[58-df-measure]]","[[58-df-measurable-space]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-product-measure"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-product-measure</span><span>Product Measure</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-product-measure — Product Measure"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"58-df-measure\">58-df-measure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"7f96c502a4a99a46\" href=\"?note=7f96c502a4a99a46\" title=\"58-df-measurable-space\">58-df-measurable-space</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I,X,\\mathcal F,\\mu_\\bullet,\\Sigma,\\mu\\in V\">\\(I,X,\\mathcal F,\\mu_\\bullet,\\Sigma,\\mu\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X:I\\to V\">\\(X:I\\to V\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal F(i)\\subseteq\\mathcal P(X(i))\">\\(\\mathcal F(i)\\subseteq\\mathcal P(X(i))\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu_\\bullet:I\\to V\">\\(\\mu_\\bullet:I\\to V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MeasurableSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MeasurableSpace}_S\\)</span> are as in the dependencies</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S\\)</span> are the four- and six-place predicates defined below</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}product\\text{-}sigma}\\vdash{}&amp;\\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S(\\Sigma,X,\\mathcal F,I)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{dom}(X)=I\\land\\operatorname{dom}(\\mathcal F)=I\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\mathrm{MeasurableSpace}_S(X(i),\\mathcal F(i))\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\Sigma=\\bigcap\\left\\{\\mathcal A\\subseteq\\mathcal P\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in I}X(i)\\right):\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}\\!\\left(\\mathcal A,\\prod_{i\\in I}X(i)\\right)\\right.\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\left.\\land\\left\\{\\prod_{i\\in I}E(i):E\\in\\prod_{i\\in I}\\mathcal F(i)\\land\\left|\\{i\\in I:E(i)\\neq X(i)\\}\\right|&lt;\\aleph_0\\right\\}\\subseteq\\mathcal A\\right\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}product\\text{-}sigma}\\vdash{}&amp;\\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S(\\Sigma,X,\\mathcal F,I)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{dom}(X)=I\\land\\operatorname{dom}(\\mathcal F)=I\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\mathrm{MeasurableSpace}_S(X(i),\\mathcal F(i))\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\Sigma=\\bigcap\\left\\{\\mathcal A\\subseteq\\mathcal P\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in I}X(i)\\right):\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}\\!\\left(\\mathcal A,\\prod_{i\\in I}X(i)\\right)\\right.\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\left.\\land\\left\\{\\prod_{i\\in I}E(i):E\\in\\prod_{i\\in I}\\mathcal F(i)\\land\\left|\\{i\\in I:E(i)\\neq X(i)\\}\\right|&lt;\\aleph_0\\right\\}\\subseteq\\mathcal A\\right\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}product\\text{-}measure} \\vdash \\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S(\\mu,\\mu_\\bullet,X,\\mathcal F,\\Sigma,I)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S(\\Sigma,X,\\mathcal F,I)\\land\\operatorname{dom}(\\mu_\\bullet)=I\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\!\\left(\\mu,\\prod_{i\\in I}X(i),\\Sigma\\right)\\land\\mu\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in I}X(i)\\right)=1\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu_\\bullet(i),X(i),\\mathcal F(i))\\land\\mu_\\bullet(i)(X(i))=1\\bigr)\\land\\forall E\\in\\prod_{i\\in I}\\mathcal F(i)\\;\\left(\\left\\lvert\\{i\\in I:E(i)\\neq X(i)\\}\\right\\rvert&lt;\\aleph_0\\to\\mu\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in I}E(i)\\right)=\\prod_{i\\in I}\\mu_\\bullet(i)(E(i))\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}product\\text{-}measure} \\vdash \\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S(\\mu,\\mu_\\bullet,X,\\mathcal F,\\Sigma,I)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S(\\Sigma,X,\\mathcal F,I)\\land\\operatorname{dom}(\\mu_\\bullet)=I\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\!\\left(\\mu,\\prod_{i\\in I}X(i),\\Sigma\\right)\\land\\mu\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in I}X(i)\\right)=1\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu_\\bullet(i),X(i),\\mathcal F(i))\\land\\mu_\\bullet(i)(X(i))=1\\bigr)\\land\\forall E\\in\\prod_{i\\in I}\\mathcal F(i)\\;\\left(\\left\\lvert\\{i\\in I:E(i)\\neq X(i)\\}\\right\\rvert&lt;\\aleph_0\\to\\mu\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in I}E(i)\\right)=\\prod_{i\\in I}\\mu_\\bullet(i)(E(i))\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Product sigma-algebra: generated by measurable rectangles</li>\n<li>Product measure: unique measure on product sigma-algebra extending rectangles</li>\n<li>Fubini's theorem: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\int_{X \\times Y} f\\,d(\\mu \\times \\nu) = \\int_X (\\int_Y f\\,d\\nu)\\,d\\mu\">\\(\\int_{X \\times Y} f\\,d(\\mu \\times \\nu) = \\int_X (\\int_Y f\\,d\\nu)\\,d\\mu\\)</span></li>\n<li>Tonelli's theorem: non-negative functions, can interchange integrals without conditions</li>\n<li>Kolmogorov extension: consistent finite-dimensional distributions extend to probability space</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Durrett, Probability: Theory and Examples</li>\n<li>Billingsley, Probability and Measure</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-measure","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-measure]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-measurable-space","status":"resolved","id":"7f96c502a4a99a46","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-measurable-space]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"I,X,\\mathcal F,\\mu_\\bullet,\\Sigma,\\mu\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"X:I\\to V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal F(i)\\subseteq\\mathcal P(X(i))","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu_\\bullet:I\\to V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Measure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MeasurableSpace}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}product\\text{-}sigma}\\vdash{}&\\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S(\\Sigma,X,\\mathcal F,I)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{dom}(X)=I\\land\\operatorname{dom}(\\mathcal F)=I\\\\\n&\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\mathrm{MeasurableSpace}_S(X(i),\\mathcal F(i))\\\\\n&\\land\\Sigma=\\bigcap\\left\\{\\mathcal A\\subseteq\\mathcal P\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in I}X(i)\\right):\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}\\!\\left(\\mathcal A,\\prod_{i\\in I}X(i)\\right)\\right.\\\\\n&\\qquad\\left.\\land\\left\\{\\prod_{i\\in I}E(i):E\\in\\prod_{i\\in I}\\mathcal F(i)\\land\\left|\\{i\\in I:E(i)\\neq X(i)\\}\\right|<\\aleph_0\\right\\}\\subseteq\\mathcal A\\right\\}.\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}product\\text{-}measure} \\vdash \\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S(\\mu,\\mu_\\bullet,X,\\mathcal F,\\Sigma,I)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S(\\Sigma,X,\\mathcal F,I)\\land\\operatorname{dom}(\\mu_\\bullet)=I\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\!\\left(\\mu,\\prod_{i\\in I}X(i),\\Sigma\\right)\\land\\mu\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in I}X(i)\\right)=1\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu_\\bullet(i),X(i),\\mathcal F(i))\\land\\mu_\\bullet(i)(X(i))=1\\bigr)\\land\\forall E\\in\\prod_{i\\in I}\\mathcal F(i)\\;\\left(\\left\\lvert\\{i\\in I:E(i)\\neq X(i)\\}\\right\\rvert<\\aleph_0\\to\\mu\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in I}E(i)\\right)=\\prod_{i\\in I}\\mu_\\bullet(i)(E(i))\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\int_{X \\times Y} f\\,d(\\mu \\times \\nu) = \\int_X (\\int_Y f\\,d\\nu)\\,d\\mu","display":false}],"bytes":2443,"backlinks":[{"id":"389a25d3cf383a61","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"2751a859d290ac09","anchor":"ref-6","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S(\\mu_\\alpha,\\mu_\\bullet,X,\\mathcal F,\\Sigma_A,\\mathbb Z)$ is the product-measure predicate (see [[58-df-product-measure]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-994","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-product-measure.md|58-df-product-measure]]（batch09）"}],"outgoing":["ca832ed6bc22f728","7f96c502a4a99a46"]}